{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/928444-house-rules-you-game-with","id":928444,"title":"\"House rules\" you game with","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-08T14:40:53-07:00","id":928444,"title":"\"House rules\" you game with","content":"When you host a game (regardless of genre, rules set etc) are there any House rules you use (NOT game specific house rules).<br /> Such as<br /> 1) all cell phones are silenced or turned off<br /> 2) keys for vehicles get left with the wife, who verifies you are not drunk before driving home<br /> (yes both of those i have seen).<br /> <br /> For me the 3 i have generally gone with are<br /> 1) as the host and usually one running the games, i get pick for chair/spot on the table. All others are first come first serve, unless someone has a medical need for a certain location..<br /> 2) as the host, and as a smoker, i Will be smoking, but if anyone's got issues with it, i will open windows/put a fan on to blow the smoke outside..<br /> 3) Cause i understand some have jobs needing you to be on call, phones will be kept in vibrate mode, but if i get to you, say in combat, and you are too busy chatting/texting etc ON Said phone, your character, is just quivering in a corner doing nothing for that round.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:51:09-07:00","id":928453,"title":"","content":"In other words, physical rules for staying in your house and playing old-style tabletop rather than any changes to mechanics or the likes?<br /> Otherwise seem reasonable enough as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T22:45:30-07:00","id":928600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/928444-house-rules-you-game-with?p=928453#post928453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, physical rules for staying in your house and playing old-style tabletop rather than any changes to mechanics or the likes?<br /> Otherwise seem reasonable enough as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Hence the &quot;House&quot; rules tag.<br /> One of the most recent i remember, was when i was in Bahrain. Since the DM did most all the rolling for us for everything our characters did (it turned out fun to play that way), one of the 2 HR's he had was don't bring dice.. If we needed to roll for something he would provide us the die to do so..<br /> His other one was based on both his wife AND daughter having a major allergy to Chocolate (gave them major rashes), so we were not allowed to bring in any food that had chocolate in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T23:59:02-07:00","id":928620,"title":"","content":"One additional rule to your opening post in our rounds is that the ST is exempt from bringing snacks, he can bring something but doesn't have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:44:43-07:00","id":929976,"title":"","content":"One house rule I have been running with recently is to ignore 1s for damage and soak rolls. I though I might help speed up combat a little, and it sure does. In my WtA game I'm running, one of my players is a Get Ahroun who routinely rolls 8+ damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/767-lostinsanity","name":"LostInSanity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:32:14-07:00","id":930029,"title":"","content":"Doesn't that ever become a problem in terms of scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T22:28:50-07:00","id":930177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostInSanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/928444-house-rules-you-game-with?p=929976#post929976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One house rule I have been running with recently is to ignore 1s for damage and soak rolls. I though I might help speed up combat a little, and it sure does. In my WtA game I'm running, one of my players is a Get Ahroun who routinely rolls 8+ damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is more of an IN game house rule. i am talking about rules you or whom ever is hosting the game, has for his or her house.. Such as, everyone brings their own food.. Shoes off at the door and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:28:28-07:00","id":930202,"title":"","content":"The cell phone rule--seconded, thirded, fourthed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T10:44:01-07:00","id":930413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/928444-house-rules-you-game-with?p=930177#post930177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is more of an IN game house rule. i am talking about rules you or whom ever is hosting the game, has for his or her house.. Such as, everyone brings their own food.. Shoes off at the door and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, guess I should have read instead of skimmed it, so on topic I don't have any 'house' rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/767-lostinsanity","name":"LostInSanity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:48:07-07:00","id":930450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostInSanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/928444-house-rules-you-game-with?p=930413#post930413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oops, guess I should have read instead of skimmed it, so on topic I don't have any 'house' rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you played at someone else's house who did have rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T19:55:38-07:00","id":930667,"title":"","content":"The only out-of-game rule I've ever had to put down with any group is no laptops or tablets while game is on. This received a little push back, as people do like using them for easy PDF reference, die rollers, and other tools, but for the most part it went over smoothly. Last week I did have to politely ask people to not play Pokemon Go at the table, but since everyone was cool about I don't know if I'd call it a &quot;rule.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T20:59:28-07:00","id":930699,"title":"","content":"I refuse to play not online these days lol<br /> <br /> I hate that I'm a smoker and if I'm somewhere I have to go outside to smoke. <br /> <br /> I am vehemently against Alchohol and hate drinking at the table it is much more bearable<br /> If I don't have to smell it <br /> <br /> I can get my own snacks and not have to worry about anyone else <br /> <br /> I could go on why I prefer online gaming but I won't<br /> <br /> However when I did play in person <br /> <br /> 1. No Alchohol or intoxicants. If you're under the influence you don't play with us <br /> 2. No texting, handhelds or laptops <br /> 3. No book flipping when an issue comes up st makes a call and we worry about it after session <br /> 4. Hourly breaks for smokers to go outside (I'm not a monster I won't pollute someone's lungs with my cancer sticks ) <br /> 5. All player rolls are made out in the open in view of everyone or it doesn't count","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","user":"Slimjimjohnson","date":". 07-13-2016, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T10:52:13-07:00","id":930938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/928444-house-rules-you-game-with?p=930450#post930450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you played at someone else's house who did have rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone I game with these days I have known for a very long time, so any such house rules are mostly just common courtesy that you would follow for anybodies house, such as smokers smoke outside, or taking your shoes off in the house.<br /> If someone wants to bring snacks, great, but it's not required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/767-lostinsanity","name":"LostInSanity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:49:25-07:00","id":954073,"title":"","content":"I'm toying with the idea of how Demon: The Fallen handles devouring of other demons. There's no real name for it, so let's call it Diablorie.<br /> <br /> - Once a demon is Diablorised it releases an amount of Faith equal to its Faith rating.<br /> - The Diablorising demon can absorb an amount of Faith up to its own Faith rating.<br /> - If not all Faith is absorbed this way it can be granted to another nearby Fallen, who too can absorb up to their Faith rating.<br /> - If all Faith is absorbed this way, the victim is destroyed. If not, the victim is sent back to the Abyss, with its Faith rating reduced to its remaining Faith and loses all dots (but not knowledge) taken by the Diabloriser..<br /> - Faith can then be spent on freebie points (as per the regular rules), knowledge (same), upgrade its Faith rating for one point (not two), or spend them to obtain a Lore the victim knew.<br /> - Learning Lores this way is a 1:1 trade, limited by what the victim knew. Upgrading their own Lores is not possible.<br /> - If the Diabloriser has the ability to cover the Pact, it can &quot;adopt&quot; one of the victim's Thralls for 1 point. Said Thrall becomes bound to its new master, with the Demon being aware of the terms and extent of the abilities granted. The Thrall does not notice any of this.<br /> - Finally, the Faith points can be converted into 5 regular XP each, which can be spent as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:32:23-07:00","id":954228,"title":"","content":"Oh god... Ok, you asked for this.<br /> <br /> Over the years, we have only really needed &quot;home rules&quot; for little things. The following are more courtesy rules and are unofficial.<br /> 1) No more than one smoke break every two hours. As I am the only smoker and the one to make the rule, it's really my own way of being courteous to others. This also happens to be used for dramatic effect; often I'll step out for a smoke break as a mini-cliffhanger, like the group just found the McGuffin, but some complication has arisen.<br /> 2) Fair division of table space. No brainer, never been much of an issue.<br /> 3) If Penny wants to get involved in the game, Penny gets involved in the game. Penny is a dog, an adorable dog, and has often added to scenes. Her participation should be acknowledged.<br /> 4) Outside talk should be kept to a minimum. Because we can get completely sidetracked about anything and everything.<br /> <br /> And that's it. But back in the day... Oh, back in the day. Waaay back when we were all younger, we had to include some very special rules. And write them out. And post them to a wall. And enforce them. I will offer no explanations and let the list speak for itself. Suffice to say, most players agreed these rules were required and very reasonable.<br /> <br /> 1) Do not urinate in the bathroom sink.<br /> 2) If you are going to spend half an hour in the bathroom without flushing the toilet, we know what you really did in there. Do not do that in this house.<br /> 3) Please shower before leaving your house.<br /> 4) Upon arrival at the game, you may be subjected to random searches of bags, pockets, and possibly more.<br /> 5) No glue or glue-like substances are allowed.<br /> 6) If you insist on cooking during food breaks, you must bring your own fire extinguisher.<br /> 7) All towels must be placed in the dirty laundry bin before leaving.<br /> 8) (Name) will be banned from utilizing the bathroom if it is found he is leaving bodily fluids in the toilet that are not human waste without flushing.<br /> 9) Any needed repairs to the property must be paid for by all responsible parties equally.<br /> 10) The DM/GM/ST is the only one allowed to use the bed, unless otherwise approved in advance.<br /> 11) Weapons are strictly prohibited indoors. Limited use outdoors is allowed if the circumstances warrant it, if an honorable duel is declared, or if any of the previous rules have been violated. In the latter case, appropriate weapons will be provided.<br /> <br /> Some sound worse than they are. Some were far worse than they sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}